# error: zero_action.grammar:23:
#
# `0` is not an element position: `→ 0` and `→ (0 1 2)` are rejected with a
# location. (README documents `0` as "the rule name as tag"; if 1.0 keeps
# that meaning instead, turn this into a run test.)
#
# Today: `→ 0` is silently ignored (default action), and `(0 1 2)` emits a
# tag literally named "0".
# (architecture.md Appendix A: nest.grammar; SPEC §3.2, §8.11)

@lexer
tokens
    ident
    eof
    err
[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser
@lang = "zero_action"

top! = item                                 → 1
item = IDENT IDENT                          → 0
     | IDENT IDENT IDENT                    → (0 1 2)
